{
  "summary": "This experiment established the search baseline by testing the simplest RNA-only configuration (single profile, PCA-2000 encoder, no image, no fusion), yielding a validation accuracy of 0.485 with a supporting F1 of 0.464. As the first completed experiment, this result serves as the performance floor for RNA-based classification and provides the reference point against which all subsequent design choices (richer RNA encoders, multiprofile aggregation, image modality, multimodal fusion) will be measured. It remains uncertain whether this accuracy is near the ceiling achievable with RNA data alone or whether substantially richer representations or additional modalities could produce meaningful gains."
}

